# Copy to .env if you need to override the backend URL - for local dev
# against Expo Go/a dev client, you normally don't need to touch this at
# all (see below). Expo inlines any EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable into the JS
# bundle at build time - never put secrets here. The mobile app has none
# to store (see docs/API.md).

# Base URL of the GawachaBazaar backend API (FastAPI), including /api/v1.
#
# By default the app derives this automatically from the same host Expo
# Go/the dev client already used to reach Metro (see
# src/api/client.ts::resolveBaseUrl) - it self-heals across DHCP/network
# changes, so a LAN IP change never breaks the app the way a hardcoded
# value would. This works for the Android emulator, iOS simulator, and a
# physical device without any per-platform configuration, as long as the
# backend runs on port 8000 on the same machine as Metro.
#
# Set EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL below only to override that - e.g. a
# production/standalone build (no Metro dev server to derive a host
# from), or a backend that isn't on port 8000 on the same machine.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://<host>:8000/api/v1
